whether a slow transport-memory field can improve local routing,
not:
whether Yggdrasil already has the final demand-gradient mechanism.

COMPARATORS

UNIFORM TRANSPORT
All edges:
conductance 1.

No transport memory.

UNDIRECTED PERMANENT REINFORCEMENT
Successful flow increases the edge's conductance.

The increase affects both directions.

No decay.

UNDIRECTED DECAYING REINFORCEMENT
Same reinforcement,
but conductance slowly relaxes toward baseline.

DIRECTED PERMANENT REINFORCEMENT
The actual flow direction is reinforced separately.

A path used:
A -> B

does not automatically reinforce:
B -> A.

No decay.

DIRECTED DECAYING REINFORCEMENT
Directional flow trace
+
slow decay toward baseline.

This is the strongest tested developmental working point.

